SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

This project's own information model, and the only one it defines.

It is shipped as a nodeset rather than created at run time, and registered and imported through
opensmi.server's nodeset handling like every standard nodeset. The namespace URI names the
information model rather than the distribution that ships it.

Two things live here:

* `BindingEventType`, the one event this project raises about itself. It subtypes `BaseEventType`
  (i=2041) rather than the house `AlertType`, which is an `AlarmConditionType` descendant and
  would promise a condition lifecycle the stack underneath does not implement.
* `SignedByteString`, a `ByteString` (i=15) subtype that says the elements packed into a bulk
  payload are signed.

The event type's three properties carry no access level, which leaves them at the default of
read-only. The house `AlertType` marks its own `ErrorCode` writable; an event field is something
a server reports and a client reads, so copying that would hand a client a write it has no
business making.

The NodeId class in smart_factory_ros2.py is generated from this file with opensmi's nodeset
generator. Re-generate it by hand whenever this file changes.
-->
